{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "id": "h200-continuation-001:H01",
      "criteria": {
        "baseline_relative_value": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Credible conditional delta: the installed objective uses \"draft_cost_ms[len(req_ids)]\", while supplied dispatch analysis identifies budget-dependent draft padding. The eight-hour offline check can establish whether this dependency matters to policy decisions. Local frequency, removable time and ITL effect remain unknown. Corrected AV must ultimately outperform AV-off k5, not merely improve the stock AV objective."
        },
        "bounded_pilot_decision": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The proposal preserves the C24 hold, starts offline, and conditions GPU work on a reviewed measurement addendum. It specifies all-rank coverage, valid timing associations, correctness, accepted progress and overhead accounting, with appropriate stop/inconclusive distinctions. GPU readiness remains conditional; the exact materiality estimator and measurement uncertainty rule still need freezing."
        },
        "engineering_time_and_fit": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Caps distinguish inspection, implementation/correctness and instrumentation: 8, 32 and 16 engineering hours, respectively. Installed paths and model_state.py provenance are identified, avoiding an engine port. Actual effort and compatibility remain unknown. The feasibility checkpoint appropriately limits work if synchronized dispatch pricing requires additional coordination."
        },
        "evaluation_gpu_budget": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Research uses zero GPU-hours. Three conditional 60-minute eight-GPU allocations correctly total 24 GPU-hours, including startup, calibration, measurement and cleanup, without automatic retries. Later service budgets are separate and monetary cost is parameterized. This qualification ceiling exceeds the proposed 20-GPU-hour screen, making the offline and intermediate stopping gates consequential."
        },
        "evidence_and_history": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 5,
          "rationale": "Reported observation: C24 says \"adaptive verification remains unqualified.\" Implementation evidence: the supplied objective contains a request-count-indexed draft term. The synthetic artifact explicitly reports \"no measured milliseconds, dispatch or service gain.\" Transfer inference: coupled dispatch pricing could improve decisions. This is a specific continuation question that preserves C03's unfavorable screen and C24's inconclusive timing."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "The synthetic budgets 11 versus 3 establish sensitivity to invented costs, not a real ranking error or benefit.",
        "Per-rank budget choices interact through DP maxima. A local counterfactual must hold other ranks' states explicit and include any extra coordination required to implement the policy.",
        "The proposed future baseline capture is justified only by a concrete instrumentation change; repeating the former capture schedule alone would not resolve its failed coverage and associations.",
        "Stock-AV improvement is insufficient if corrected AV still loses to fixed-k5 AV-off after accepted-progress and controller costs."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Retain the offline-first disposition. Before GPU qualification, freeze the instrumentation repair, joint-rank dispatch reconstruction, policy-comparison units and uncertainty/materiality rule. Make the advancement comparison explicitly include AV-off k5, stock AV and the locked static policy. Treat this as the existing C24 continuation work item, with no automatic repeat or full-attempt allocation."
    },
    {
      "id": "h200-continuation-001:H02",
      "criteria": {
        "baseline_relative_value": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "The installed \"for i in range(n_spec):\" loop and proposed fusion provide a plausible path to shortening repeated draft sampling work. The four-hour gate audit can resolve baseline eligibility before implementation. The card correctly compares graph against graph and retains the bias GEMM. Eligible frequency, exposed sampling cost and local effect size remain unknown."
        },
        "bounded_pilot_decision": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The staged audit, component test and all-rank integration can distinguish incompatibility, correctness failure, immaterial savings and inadequate evidence. Real weights, RNG identity, scratch lifetime, watermark preservation and native opportunity coverage are addressed. Passing cheap inspection would qualify further design work; it would not establish that the incomplete kernel is ready to port."
        },
        "engineering_time_and_fit": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "The 4-hour inspection, 32-hour implementation/correctness and 10-hour instrumentation caps are explicit, with an early feasibility stop. Actual port feasibility remains unknown: the supplied patch omits completion/reduction and launcher details, and weight access is gated by specialized decode. A safe independent adapter on SM90 is proposed, not established."
        },
        "evaluation_gpu_budget": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The future envelope is correctly charged: 45 minutes plus two 60-minute eight-GPU allocations equals 22 GPU-hours. Compilation, graph capture, startup and cleanup are included; cap exhaustion is inconclusive and retries are excluded. CPU inspection precedes allocation. Later screen, confirmation and held-out costs remain separate."
        },
        "evidence_and_history": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Implementation evidence includes \"and self.draft_watermarker is None\" and the specialized weight-access gate. PR61869's GB300 results are author-reported bundle measurements; its tests state \"The Markov weights are integer-valued\". Transfer inference is limited to an isolated SM90 fusion. The card preserves these limitations and distinguishes sampling fusion from the held C03 padding mechanism."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "Baseline watermarking being enabled does not establish whether the draft watermarker is active. Eligibility is unknown, not a demonstrated contract violation.",
        "The omitted arrival-counter reduction and launcher code contains material synchronization and scratch-reuse details; the supplied excerpt cannot establish their correctness.",
        "Integer-weight upstream parity does not establish parity with actual checkpoint weights, vocabulary mappings or the installed probability cache.",
        "Positive component savings could still be too small after graph execution, fallback frequency and resource contention to justify a service attempt."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Keep the four-hour gate audit eligible. Before implementation, supply the complete pinned fusion/launcher source and document an adapter independent of specialized decode. Resolve draft watermark ownership and all constructor predicates. Freeze real-weight parity tolerances, measurement uncertainty and native-exposure materiality rules before releasing the conditional GPU budget."
    },
    {
      "id": "h200-continuation-001:H03",
      "criteria": {
        "baseline_relative_value": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Repeated eligible router GEMMs could shorten verification steps while preserving Marlin and transport. The three-hour loader/dtype/dispatch inspection is an appropriate cheap test of whether any baseline delta exists. FP32 output alone does not establish FP32 weights or active SGEMM execution. Local exposure and ITL benefit remain unknown."
        },
        "bounded_pilot_decision": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "The plan separates eligibility, exact-shape component tests and all-rank integration, with coverage thresholds and meaningful numerical, routing and changed-math quality checks. It preserves the fastest legal installed comparator and frozen service gates. The phrase \"An absent eligible branch is established\" is ambiguous and should distinguish an active eligible baseline branch from an absent optimization."
        },
        "engineering_time_and_fit": {
          "verdict": "unknown",
          "score": 3,
          "rationale": "Inspection and implementation are capped, but actual fit is unresolved: only nominal router construction and a PR description are supplied; installed loader/forward code and the proposed kernel are absent. SM90 hardware correspondence supports inspection, not integration readiness. Clarify whether the four-hour feasibility checkpoint is included within the twenty-hour implementation cap."
        },
        "evaluation_gpu_budget": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Thirty minutes plus two 60-minute eight-GPU allocations correctly totals 20 GPU-hours. Startup, JIT, capture, tests and cleanup are included, with no automatic retries. The short standalone slot may expire during compilation, but the declared inconclusive outcome handles that uncertainty. Research remains zero-GPU and later service costs are separate."
        },
        "evidence_and_history": {
          "verdict": "pass",
          "score": 4,
          "rationale": "Nominal implementation evidence is limited to \"out_dtype=torch.float32,\" and hash-routing construction. PR61903 claims \"a CuteDSL BF16x3 kernel for SM90\" and reports H200 tests on other shapes/models. Transfer inference to this service remains conditional on loaded dtype and dispatch. The proposal correctly preserves C01's externally reported grouped hold and does not equate router optimization with expert-backend replacement."
        }
      },
      "factual_support": "pass",
      "objections": [
        "Neither eligible FP32 weights nor active learned-router GEMM calls are established by the supplied constructor.",
        "Hash-routing state does not by itself quantify bypass frequency or prove the installed forward path.",
        "Cold-L2 H200 microbenchmarks and other-model results cannot establish savings at native DeepSeek graph shapes and cache conditions.",
        "Lower average numerical error does not guarantee unchanged near-tied expert choices, downstream work or quality."
      ],
      "required_revision": "Retain the three-hour eligibility audit. Rewrite the support condition to require an active eligible baseline branch and an absent equivalent optimization. Before implementation, identify installed loader/dispatch hashes and the exact proposed kernel revision, clarify the engineering subtotal, and freeze local-shape timing, numerical and quality acceptance rules."
    }
  ],
  "global_gaps": [
    "The requested four-candidate deliverable contains only three cards. This is a completeness shortfall, not a reason to fail the three supplied mechanisms. The brief DeepInfer PR54 inspection note lacks a complete fourth candidate design.",
    "Required-criterion passes above concern bounded qualification plans. No candidate has demonstrated local savings or earned either remaining full service attempt. Unknown implementation fit does not prevent the explicitly capped source inspections.",
    "All local candidate effect sizes, exposed savings and realized implementation effort remain unknown. The stated order is a diagnostic priority, not an evidence-backed ranking of net service benefit.",
    "Before future GPU allocation, freeze pilot measurement units, repetitions, uncertainty handling and the rule connecting native incidence and net component savings to plausible materiality. Opportunity counts alone are not sufficient.",
    "Full G01-G05 and Q01-Q04 definitions and underlying raw artifacts are not supplied. Proposed checks are useful, but completed correctness qualification cannot be inferred from their names or historical scoped C03 checks.",
    "Preserve C03's valid unfavorable screen, C01's missing raw grouped evidence and C24's completed instrumentation-inconclusive diagnostic. The supplied history supports continuation design, not a duplicate runtime campaign or a reset of prior outcomes.",
    "Supplied DeepInfer PR bodies and pinned controller excerpts support limited engineering analysis. Missing issue bodies, PR comments, complete kernels and paper sections remain unknown; links and fulltext metadata do not supply those contents. DeepInfer production claims do not establish matched H200 EP4 performance.",
    "The future pilot ceilings total 66 GPU-hours if all three advance. They are conditional alternatives, not an allocated portfolio. Node price and cost-per-token gains remain unknown; fixed-load throughput cannot establish capacity gains.",
    "This review used only supplied text. No tools, file modifications, agents, CPU tests or GPU execution were used; reported experiments were not independently rechecked."
  ]
}
